{
 "elemod": 2,
 "id": "core",
 "version": "0.11",
 "title": "core",
 "description": "The boot copier, the hook bus, mod storage and parameter pages for the Analog Rytm MKII: every other mod needs it. The Digitakt mk1's core.s, settings.s and render.s with the Rytm's addresses, and store.c: fields mods declare, placed by elekloader from the build's lockfile and kept in bytes stock never uses or always holds at 0; and pages.s: parameter pages and parameter overrides mods add through the tables core_pages and core_params (and core_page_fns, a page whose knobs follow the sound), from the first instructions of the four routines a page goes through, and the page keys' lists, stock's pages and then the ones mods add through core_view_pages, which the page key steps through (skipping a page while its mod says it is hidden, with the page's title in the header), and which keeps its page when the view is shown again; load.s: the audio interrupt's load, core_audio_load, for mods with work they can skip; and machines.c: machines mods add in the hidden slots 34..43 through core_machines, written into the machine table and the slots' parameter records at boot; and lock.c and lock.s (0.8): lockable parameters, sound fields with lock codes from the lockfile that mods register in core_lock_params, listed as LFO destinations (core_lfo_offset) and taken by RANDOMIZE PAGE and RELOAD PAGE; and rows.c and rows.s (0.8): their p-locks, as lock rows with their codes in each pattern's row pool, set with a trig held and read by mods while the trig plays (core_lock_value); and scenes.c and scenes.s (0.8): their scene locks and performance depths, as entries with their codes in each kit's lists, set with a pad held in scene or performance edit and read by mods (core_scene_value, core_perf_offset). And midi.c and midi.s (0.8): their NRPNs (MSB 4, LSB the code - 42) and, for the first 33 codes, CCs from the 33 stock leaves unused, taken in on a track's channel and sent when a mod's knob turns one. On its own it changes nothing the unit does. And smooth.c (0.9): the value stock would play for a lockable parameter (core_param_value), its target (the sound, a p-lock, a scene lock) smoothed with stock's one-pole and the performances and the LFO added after, computed only when a mod reads it; a field declared \"smooth\": false jumps. And routes.c and routes.s (0.9): a lockable parameter declared \"mod\": true as a destination in each sound's VELOCITY MOD and AFTERTOUCH lists, the route keeping its code in its own byte, shown on its knob, taken out of stock's apply and handed to the mod (core_mod_offset), and added in core_param_value. And the FX track (0.9): a lockable kit field is the FX track's parameter, an FX LFO destination (core_fx_lfo_dst keeps its code), p-locked, locked in scenes and performances and on MIDI on the FX track, read with track 12; and a code an LFO points to no longer reaches the stored sound or kit through stock's edit write (st_sound_through, st_fx_through). And finish.s (0.7): an OS upgrade's restart sends the panel link's and the UART's queued bytes before it masks interrupts, where stock can hang on SUCCESS! REBOOTING. And ev_project_save (0.10): f(pre, how) before and after every whole save of the live project to a +Drive slot (SAVE PROJECT, SAVE PROJECT AS, the project menu's saves, an empty slot's LOAD), with the kind of save and the slot; a field set before the save is in the saved copy. And (0.10) core_param_value at about a quarter of 0.9's cost, and core_param_handle and core_param_value_h to read by a handle. And (0.11) p-locks a mod keeps itself: a knob id from 555 in a core_param_locks entry gets stock's lock calls with the track and step, its label and name, live recording's step, and core_held_step for its text. And (0.11) step tags: a mod's 16-bit handle on each step of each pattern (core_step_owners, core_step_tag, core_step_tag_set, core_step_tags), kept in RAM and moved wherever stock moves the step, with ev_steps telling the mod what moved, dropped, reloaded or changed length. And (0.11) the moments: ev_sysex_in (a SysEx message in, which a mod may take), core_midi_try_send (USB MIDI out that never waits), the UI's current kit, track and pattern with their items, ev_kit (a kit selected or pushed to the engine; a stopped kit change drops the playing trig's mod locks), the live project's name, \"handle\": true storage fields walked by core_handle_fields, and ev_project_slot (a +Drive slot cleared, initialized or pasted outside a save). And (0.11) the sequencer: ev_seq_step (the tracks that reached a step this tick and those whose next step trigs, from the clock, with the first step after PLAY seeded), ev_seq_tick (each clock tick), ev_transport (the play state changed), and core_transport, core_pattern_now, core_pattern_next, core_tempo, core_track_speed and core_track_step.",
 "category": "Framework",
 "author": "irpina, Iced-Cream",
 "license": "GPL-2.0-or-later",
 "target": {
  "device": "analog-rytm-mk2",
  "product": "Analog Rytm MKII",
